# Intentionally empty. The real-IP directives that used to be here are in
# 00-realip.conf.template now, chosen per LISTEN_MODE.
#
# Why this file still exists: nginx's container renders the templates into
# /etc/nginx/conf.d/ every time it starts, but never deletes what an earlier
# start rendered. A container that ran before the move still has the old
# conf.d/00-cloudflare-realip.conf, full of directives, and a plain
# `docker compose restart nginx` would load it next to 00-realip.conf. nginx
# then refuses to start ("real_ip_header directive is duplicate"). Rendering
# this empty file overwrites the old one, so a restart is safe.
#
# It can be deleted once nginx has been RECREATED (not just restarted) on
# every server since the move: `docker compose up -d --force-recreate nginx`.
